Glossary:

- skill (מיומנות): a specific topic like פירוק טרינום
- exercise (תרגיל): a qustion on a certain topic, can be either open ended or multiple choice
- lesson (שיעור): set of skills like טכניקה אלגברית 1
- quiz (בוחן): a test on a single lesson, can be retaken, best grade wins. each retake draws new questions
- exrcise test (מבחן תרגול): a timed test on a set of a lessons, can be retaken, best grade wins
- simulation test (מבחן סימלוציה): a timed test on a set of a lessons, one time only
- test: real life test, appears in app as a date + the lessons it covers. set by the teacher



Goals:

The app helps the student to:
1. master the skills - done by the path
2. get ready for the real life tests - done by the test countdown plan



Goal 1: Mastering the skills (the path)

Each skill goes through these stages:
1. worked example: the student sees a full solution and is asked "why this step?"
2. faded examples: steps are removed one at a time, the student fills them in
3. practice: immediate feedback that names the specific mistake.
   after a wrong answer, the student gets a similar question (not the same one)
4. mastered: 3 correct answers in a row, without hints, across at least 2 different days

Skill states:
- not started
- learning
- mastered
- needs review: a mastered skill becomes "needs review" after some days without practice

Path rules:
- the lesson's quiz (בוחן) unlocks the next lesson
- daily review: a short mixed set of "needs review" skills from different lessons



Goal 2: Getting ready for the real test

The teacher sets the test date and the lessons it covers.
The app plans backwards from the date:

- 3+ weeks before: finish the path for all the covered lessons
- 1-3 weeks before: exercise tests (מבחן תרגול) - timed, mixing all the covered lessons.
  each result points back to the weak skills in the path
- final week: simulation test (מבחן סימלוציה) - required. one attempt,
  same length and timing as the real test
- last days: targeted review of the skills that failed in the simulation,
  light mixed review the day before

Readiness meter (per test):
- % of the covered skills that are mastered
- recent exercise test grades
- simulation test grade



Student Screen:
- home
  - my assignments (המשימות שלי): homewords submitted by the teacher
  - remider on the upcoming test: days left, readiness meter, today's task
  -

- path
- grades
- collection



Teacher Screen:
- assignments
  - give an assignment. load it from:
    - the computer (file upload)
    - the board
    - a picture (camera)
  - check assignments: review each student's submitted answers and give feedback/grade
- tests
  - set a real life test: date + the lessons it covers
  - see who took the required simulation test
- class heat map
  - rows: students, columns: skills
  - each cell is colored by the skill state (not started / learning / mastered / needs review)
  - period filter: sep-dec, dec-jun
